WEBVTT

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:01.180
Last time on...

00:00:01.390 --> 00:00:02.810
<i>Love Live! Sunshine!!</i>

00:00:02.850 --> 00:00:03.690
Here we go!

00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:07.190
Mari-<i>san</i> turned down a request
to become the new school's director.

00:00:07.190 --> 00:00:09.070
After graduating from this school,

00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:11.940
I'll go to the college in Italy
that my dad recommends.

00:00:12.110 --> 00:00:15.320
After their graduation,
the third years will go their separate ways.

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:18.910
So they decided to go find a shooting star,
like they did when they were small.

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:21.970
You thought we could do anything
if the three of us were together, right?

00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:25.370
A star that's just for us...

00:00:25.370 --> 00:00:28.920
The car moves forward
with their feelings in tow.

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:33.720
That's good. Be careful with that.

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:35.470
Chika-<i>chan</i>, is your side ready?

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:37.180
There.

00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:39.640
This side is good to go. Secure it now.

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:41.550
Here we go!

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:45.650
It's done!

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:48.310
It looks great.

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:49.520
Yep!

00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:54.030
Let's show our appreciation
for this school by partying till we drop!

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:58.030
"School Closing Festival"

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:56.140
Aye, aye!

00:00:59.830 --> 00:01:13.210
<i>Let's throw our all at each other</i>
<i>and grab hold of the future!</i>

00:01:18.390 --> 00:01:23.850
<i>The sky and this ocean are both on our side</i>

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:27.810
<i>Shining and saying, "Go, do your best!"</i>

00:01:28.980 --> 00:01:34.530
<i>To let our voices reach far, far away</i>

00:01:34.530 --> 00:01:39.450
<i>Shall we shout our dreams louder?</i>

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:41.200
<i>(Full of hope)</i>

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:45.540
<i>Today pulls tomorrow toward itself</i>

00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:54.130
<i>It's really fun to grasp the magnet</i>
<i>in my heart and run right now!</i>

00:01:54.130 --> 00:01:56.260
<i>(Let's always go together)</i>

00:01:56.260 --> 00:01:59.050
<i>What shall we do about the future?!</i>

00:01:59.050 --> 00:02:06.850
<i>Everyone laughs and cries</i>
<i>as</i> <i>they</i> <i>look for the shape of their dreams</i>

00:02:06.850 --> 00:02:15.280
<i>Because I'm sure the</i> <i>future</i> <i>us</i>
<i>will have the answer</i>

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:23.370
<i>Let's run with everything we have</i>
<i>and become the shining wind</i>

00:02:23.370 --> 00:02:26.700
<i>We got dream</i>

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:29.370
"School Idol C̶u̶l̶b̶ Club"

00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:31.000
It's finally finished!

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:31.000
"School Idol C̶u̶l̶b̶ Club"
"#11 'Uranohoshi Girls' High School'"

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:32.880
"#11 'Uranohoshi Girls' High School'"

00:02:32.380 --> 00:02:38.420
My new dish has been born!
It's Stewshine Premium!

00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:42.010
Could you not cook in our club room?

00:02:42.010 --> 00:02:45.890
But everyone says that
they want to eat it again, so...

00:02:45.890 --> 00:02:50.770
School directors don't usually open a shop
in school festivals to start with!

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:53.810
Non, non, non, Dia.

00:02:53.810 --> 00:02:56.780
It's not a school festival.
It's a school closing festival.

00:02:56.780 --> 00:03:01.070
Even the director wants
to do something for the last festival.

00:03:01.070 --> 00:03:04.530
Jeez... But is it really okay...

00:03:04.870 --> 00:03:07.200
...to do this in the third term
when the students are so busy?

00:03:07.410 --> 00:03:12.670
Of course! Because everyone at school said...

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:16.170
"Request to hold a school closing festival"

00:03:13.630 --> 00:03:15.760
...that they want to hold
a school closing festival!

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:18.760
Is this...

00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:21.050
This is how we're feeling.

00:03:21.050 --> 00:03:24.050
When we asked everyone,
they said they wanted to do it, too.

00:03:24.050 --> 00:03:27.310
We didn't think the graduation ceremony
would be the appropriate time, so...

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:30.640
But since our school is closing,
we want to hold a huge festive event

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:35.310
involving graduates and
people in the neighborhood as well.

00:03:36.110 --> 00:03:37.940
We understand that
the third term is a busy time,

00:03:37.940 --> 00:03:39.900
as third years have
college entrance exams and such.

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:41.790
But this is our last chance, so...

00:03:42.490 --> 00:03:43.740
Shiny...

00:03:45.070 --> 00:03:47.330
Approoooooved!

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:50.540
"Approved"

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:50.540
What?

00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:56.170
Really... All the students
at this school are wonderful!

00:03:57.710 --> 00:03:58.980
Mari-<i>chan</i>!

00:03:59.550 --> 00:04:02.380
The arch has been set up without a hitch!

00:04:02.380 --> 00:04:07.010
Thank you! Then go back to your posts
and work on the preparations.

00:04:07.010 --> 00:04:10.100
The preparations are behind schedule overall.

00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:12.940
At this rate, we can't finish it
before night comes.

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:15.150
Yes, ma'am!

00:04:15.150 --> 00:04:16.650
Let's go!

00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:19.230
They seem to be having fun.

00:04:19.230 --> 00:04:25.210
They're happy, too, that their
schoolmates created this opportunity.

00:04:26.070 --> 00:04:27.390
I understand.

00:04:27.910 --> 00:04:30.370
We're going to take all the hopes
and feelings we had for this school

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:35.120
and throw them all into this festival...
That's the idea, right?

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:35.920
Yes.

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:41.460
In that case, I'll put aside my position
as Student Council President

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:44.010
and focus all my energy on this event!

00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:46.930
Sis! The preparation here is going perfectly!

00:04:46.930 --> 00:04:48.360
Any problems with that?

00:04:49.390 --> 00:04:51.720
"Approved"

00:04:53.730 --> 00:04:57.100
We won't make it like this! Where's Ruby?

00:04:57.350 --> 00:05:00.610
Since Ruby-<i>chan</i> is popular,
she's wanted everywhere, <i>zura</i>.

00:05:00.610 --> 00:05:03.320
So it's up to the not-so-popular
to work hard here, <i>zura</i>.

00:05:03.740 --> 00:05:05.070
What do you mean by that?

00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:09.530
What was that?

00:05:09.530 --> 00:05:11.830
I've seen them somewhere before, <i>zura</i>.

00:05:13.370 --> 00:05:14.120
Whoa!

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:16.250
Things are really coming along!

00:05:16.540 --> 00:05:18.460
Oh, hi, you're back.

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:21.800
So you're helping us, too, huh, Ruby-<i>chan</i>?

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:25.220
Yep. I've always wanted to make
this kind of costume, too, so...

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:26.970
Check this out.

00:05:26.970 --> 00:05:28.260
How cute!

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:30.260
That's amazing, Ruby-<i>chan</i>!

00:05:30.260 --> 00:05:31.180
Hm?

00:05:34.220 --> 00:05:36.060
That's You-<i>chan</i>, right?

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:38.270
Who's the other one?

00:05:40.150 --> 00:05:41.440
You-<i>chan</i>!

00:05:45.610 --> 00:05:48.070
Hm? Where did they go?

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:50.870
I thought they came this way.

00:05:50.870 --> 00:05:51.910
They disappeared, <i>zura</i>?!

00:05:51.910 --> 00:05:52.620
What?

00:05:54.160 --> 00:05:55.410
N-Now we're seeing...

00:05:55.410 --> 00:05:56.710
...ghosts, <i>zura</i>?

00:05:56.710 --> 00:05:57.820
What?!

00:06:02.420 --> 00:06:04.710
Did it really go in here?

00:06:04.710 --> 00:06:07.050
Yeah, I'm sure of it.

00:06:07.050 --> 00:06:08.840
What is this place?

00:06:09.090 --> 00:06:11.220
The fallen angel is scared, <i>zura</i>?

00:06:11.220 --> 00:06:12.810
N-N-No way!

00:06:12.810 --> 00:06:16.100
On the contrary, this dark emanation
is quite the pleasant sensation.

00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:22.730
I shall ensure everyone's safety
from here by erecting a barrier!

00:06:22.730 --> 00:06:25.030
--You're one wimpy fallen angel.
--Don't call me wimpy!

00:06:29.740 --> 00:06:31.490
Ch-Chika-<i>chan</i>...!

00:06:31.700 --> 00:06:33.880
--Hm?
--What do we do?

00:06:34.580 --> 00:06:35.490
What?

00:06:37.290 --> 00:06:40.960
But that <i>is</i> just a sheet, right?

00:06:41.790 --> 00:06:43.450
I'll check it.

00:06:44.090 --> 00:06:45.270
Be careful.

00:06:46.170 --> 00:06:49.550
Hiyaaaa!

00:06:54.010 --> 00:06:55.060
Are you okay?!

00:06:58.420 --> 00:06:59.480
What the...?

00:06:59.770 --> 00:07:03.770
Oh, it's Shiitake-<i>chan</i>... Wait, what?

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:06.730
--Of course it wasn't a ghost.
--I-I'd be okay if I had time
to mentally prepare...

00:07:06.730 --> 00:07:08.580
--Right.
--I-I'd be okay if I had time
to mentally prepare...

00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:13.810
--Ahhhhhh!
--Ahhhhhh!

00:07:14.830 --> 00:07:16.870
Wait, Shiitake!

00:07:21.870 --> 00:07:24.460
"School Closing Festival"

00:07:30.380 --> 00:07:37.260
"Approved"

00:07:30.720 --> 00:07:33.680
That incident caused a lot of damage.

00:07:33.680 --> 00:07:37.260
For the arch alone, it'll require ten people
to spend four hours repairing it.

00:07:37.260 --> 00:07:38.560
But...

00:07:38.560 --> 00:07:41.890
Why the heck was Shiitake-<i>chan</i>
at school in the first place?

00:07:41.890 --> 00:07:44.190
I heard that when
Mito-<i>nee</i> was taking a walk,

00:07:44.190 --> 00:07:46.400
she accidently let go of the leash.

00:07:46.400 --> 00:07:50.400
I don't need to hear your excuses.
In any case, how do we deal with this delay?

00:07:50.400 --> 00:07:52.620
The school closing festival is tomorrow!

00:07:52.620 --> 00:07:54.070
I'll do my best.

00:07:54.370 --> 00:07:56.620
Do you think your best is enough?

00:07:56.620 --> 00:07:59.540
It's almost time for you to go home.

00:07:59.540 --> 00:08:02.370
The last bus is coming soon, <i>zura</i>.

00:08:02.370 --> 00:08:04.670
I wonder if we can finish the preparations...

00:08:04.670 --> 00:08:05.920
Yeah.

00:08:06.250 --> 00:08:07.420
Okay.

00:08:07.420 --> 00:08:12.840
In that case, the Ohara family will
take responsibility and take you all home.

00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:13.970
Really, <i>zura</i>?!

00:08:13.970 --> 00:08:15.890
But what do you mean by "all"?

00:08:15.890 --> 00:08:18.810
All the students who remain at school
to work on the preparations.

00:08:18.810 --> 00:08:21.810
But, of course,
you'll need to let your families know.

00:08:23.100 --> 00:08:26.200
Thank you! I'll go let the others know!

00:08:28.110 --> 00:08:29.530
Are you serious?

00:08:29.530 --> 00:08:31.940
It's the last event. Let me do it.

00:08:31.940 --> 00:08:34.860
I didn't say I wouldn't let you.

00:08:34.860 --> 00:08:37.240
I suspected you were
going to do that anyway.

00:08:43.250 --> 00:08:45.080
Here! Thanks for waiting!

00:08:45.580 --> 00:08:47.080
What's this?

00:08:47.080 --> 00:08:50.340
Chika-<i>chan</i>'s family's specialty,
mandarin orange hot pot!

00:08:50.340 --> 00:08:52.840
Mito-<i>nee</i> brought this as a token of apology.

00:08:53.220 --> 00:08:56.050
If we can eat
such a delicious-looking hot pot,

00:08:56.050 --> 00:08:58.350
she can let go of the leash every day.

00:08:58.350 --> 00:09:00.010
That's a bit too much.

00:09:00.010 --> 00:09:01.270
Seconds, please, <i>zura</i>!

00:09:01.270 --> 00:09:04.350
At any rate, why in the world
are you wearing it?

00:09:04.350 --> 00:09:07.520
Well, You and I wanted to make
the classroom look like the ocean

00:09:07.520 --> 00:09:12.280
for the school closing festival,
so we decided to wear these.

00:09:12.740 --> 00:09:14.280
That means...

00:09:14.530 --> 00:09:16.030
This is You?

00:09:18.660 --> 00:09:20.740
Hey! Say something!

00:09:20.950 --> 00:09:22.700
That was a fuss over nothing, <i>zura</i>.

00:09:22.700 --> 00:09:26.500
Please don't go out in that
until the event starts.

00:09:26.500 --> 00:09:27.660
Okay, okay.

00:09:28.670 --> 00:09:30.360
Like I said, say something!

00:09:34.260 --> 00:09:36.090
The head came off, <i>zura</i>.

00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:40.430
"School Closing Festival"

00:09:39.390 --> 00:09:40.430
Oomph!

00:09:41.810 --> 00:09:43.170
Finished.

00:09:52.110 --> 00:09:54.230
School Idol Club!

00:09:54.740 --> 00:09:56.780
Please join!

00:09:56.780 --> 00:10:03.070
You and you! You want to try
being a school idol?!

00:10:06.750 --> 00:10:09.880
Yes! I'll be a school idol!

00:10:12.750 --> 00:10:13.800
Alley-oop.

00:10:14.800 --> 00:10:16.630
It's kinda quiet, isn't it?

00:10:17.300 --> 00:10:19.320
Even though it's lively
inside the school building...

00:10:20.180 --> 00:10:23.510
Yeah. It's kinda nice, isn't it?

00:10:23.510 --> 00:10:26.480
"Tea"

00:10:24.060 --> 00:10:25.980
It's normal out here,

00:10:25.980 --> 00:10:30.970
but that building is filled with everyone's
dreams and excitement for tomorrow.

00:10:31.440 --> 00:10:33.790
We even lose track of time.

00:10:34.980 --> 00:10:37.110
I like that sort of thing.

00:10:39.030 --> 00:10:41.320
I wish this would last forever.

00:10:41.910 --> 00:10:45.090
Tomorrow... the day
after tomorrow... and forever...

00:10:46.160 --> 00:10:49.070
Then... Then...

00:10:52.330 --> 00:10:55.880
You know... I've always admired you.

00:10:57.460 --> 00:11:00.120
I wanted to see what you were seeing.

00:11:01.010 --> 00:11:03.640
I wanted to see the same scenery
you were seeing forever.

00:11:04.390 --> 00:11:07.960
Shall we continue
until we all become old ladies?

00:11:12.270 --> 00:11:13.080
Yep!

00:11:22.160 --> 00:11:24.450
"School Closing Festival"

00:11:25.780 --> 00:11:28.380
--We'll see you later, Miss.
--We'll see you later, Miss.

00:11:29.540 --> 00:11:32.000
You look really good in that, Riko-<i>chan</i>.

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:33.960
Did you request it yourself?

00:11:33.960 --> 00:11:37.090
Yeah. I've always wanted
to wear an outfit like this.

00:11:37.090 --> 00:11:39.510
You look cute, too. It suits you.

00:11:39.510 --> 00:11:41.590
Really? Thanks!

00:11:41.840 --> 00:11:46.930
By the way, this was a huge help
when sewing your outfit.

00:11:44.430 --> 00:11:46.930
"Chin-in-Hand Move"
"Taisho Romanticism Edition"

00:11:47.010 --> 00:11:51.770
Ahhh! That, uh, was just something
that happened to be lying around the house!

00:11:51.770 --> 00:11:52.980
Riko-<i>chan</i>?

00:11:52.980 --> 00:11:57.110
Chika! Riko! It's about time
to change shifts, right?

00:11:57.270 --> 00:11:59.490
Why don't you go check things out?

00:11:59.490 --> 00:12:00.780
Really?!

00:12:00.780 --> 00:12:02.840
Do you wanna come with me, Riko-<i>chan</i>?

00:12:03.240 --> 00:12:06.700
I'm sorry. There's something
I need to do, so...

00:12:09.450 --> 00:12:15.040
"Uchicchi"

00:12:09.660 --> 00:12:15.040
Hello kids! Welcome to
Uranohoshi Aquarium! How are you?!

00:12:15.040 --> 00:12:16.630
Good!

00:12:16.630 --> 00:12:17.800
Okay!

00:12:17.800 --> 00:12:21.480
This is the vast deep sea of Uchiura.

00:12:26.470 --> 00:12:29.220
Wow! What a big crowd!

00:12:29.350 --> 00:12:32.430
Well then, next question!

00:12:33.190 --> 00:12:36.440
Th-The next question
gives you twice as many points.

00:12:36.560 --> 00:12:39.070
--Whoa!
--What's the correct answer?

00:12:39.070 --> 00:12:40.690
Do your Rubesty, everyone!

00:12:40.690 --> 00:12:42.150
Here's the question!

00:12:40.690 --> 00:12:48.660
"Love Live!! Quiz"

00:12:42.150 --> 00:12:45.410
What is the name of
the school idol duo from Fukuoka

00:12:45.410 --> 00:12:48.660
who performed in the second Love Live
and advanced to the finals?

00:12:49.410 --> 00:12:50.160
Mentaifo!

00:12:50.160 --> 00:12:51.190
Hakattana!

00:12:51.190 --> 00:12:52.210
Tenjintwo!

00:12:53.290 --> 00:12:57.540
Bzzzzt! Bzzzzt! Bzzzzt!

00:12:57.540 --> 00:12:59.710
The correct answer is Dream!

00:13:00.500 --> 00:13:03.970
You still have a long way to go
to be a Love Live expert.

00:13:03.970 --> 00:13:05.590
That's my sis for you!

00:13:07.140 --> 00:13:10.710
I guess Dia-<i>san</i> really likes Love Live.

00:13:13.810 --> 00:13:16.770
Would you be interested
in fortune-telling, <i>zura</i>?

00:13:16.770 --> 00:13:18.440
Hanamaru... -<i>chan</i>?

00:13:19.730 --> 00:13:22.740
You aren't interested
in fortune-telling, <i>zura</i>?

00:13:22.740 --> 00:13:24.400
Err...

00:13:27.740 --> 00:13:30.240
Welcome, my lost little demon.

00:13:30.450 --> 00:13:32.410
So this is what you guys were doing.

00:13:32.410 --> 00:13:36.170
Confide in me your troubles, and bam!
I'll make them go away!

00:13:40.420 --> 00:13:43.510
I see. Your troubles revolve around
a relationship, yes?

00:13:43.510 --> 00:13:44.970
Nope, nothing like that.

00:13:44.970 --> 00:13:49.050
Actually, we're the ones who have troubles...
getting customers, <i>zura</i>.

00:13:49.140 --> 00:13:52.850
Th-Then, you've been gaining weight recently
and you're worried that--

00:13:52.850 --> 00:13:54.350
No, no worries there.

00:13:54.350 --> 00:13:56.100
That's you, Yoshiko-<i>chan</i>, <i>zura</i>.

00:13:56.100 --> 00:13:58.940
Silence, Zuramaru! And it's Yohane!

00:13:59.150 --> 00:14:03.070
Isn't it faster if you just ask her
what she wants to know about, <i>zura</i>?

00:14:03.070 --> 00:14:05.030
Shut up! I need not ask,

00:14:05.030 --> 00:14:09.200
for the fallen angel inside me
whispers to me and tells me all!

00:14:09.200 --> 00:14:11.950
Well, anyway, I shall proceed
to reveal your fortune!

00:14:11.950 --> 00:14:13.660
Music!

00:14:15.040 --> 00:14:16.280
Whoa!

00:14:18.210 --> 00:14:20.420
You guys really went all out!

00:14:20.670 --> 00:14:22.590
So why do I have to...?

00:14:23.050 --> 00:14:24.550
Riko-<i>chan</i>?

00:14:24.550 --> 00:14:27.550
Riko-<i>chan</i> came to help us on her own.

00:14:27.550 --> 00:14:29.930
Just what we'd expect
from little demon Lili, <i>zura</i>.

00:14:29.930 --> 00:14:31.350
You did, too. You said

00:14:31.350 --> 00:14:34.720
that you wanted to help Yoshiko-<i>chan</i>
make her wish come true for once.

00:14:34.720 --> 00:14:36.950
Well, I just happened to...

00:14:37.600 --> 00:14:40.150
Zuramaru... Lili...

00:14:40.150 --> 00:14:43.940
Ah...! Then please tell Aqours' fortune...

00:14:43.940 --> 00:14:47.650
Tell me what future awaits us.

00:14:50.410 --> 00:14:52.700
For that, I need not
even bother with divination.

00:14:53.160 --> 00:14:55.660
All of my little demons are whispering...

00:14:56.500 --> 00:14:58.210
...that the future of Aqours is...

00:14:58.910 --> 00:15:04.040
"Stewshine Premium"

00:14:59.750 --> 00:15:04.040
Everyone! The director's specialty
Stewshine Premium is over here!

00:15:07.550 --> 00:15:10.470
Wow... There are so many people...

00:15:10.470 --> 00:15:13.480
Hm...? Shima-<i>nee</i> and Mito-<i>nee</i>?!

00:15:14.100 --> 00:15:15.220
Chika-<i>chan</i>!

00:15:15.220 --> 00:15:16.430
You came!

00:15:16.430 --> 00:15:17.510
Wanna have some?

00:15:18.270 --> 00:15:20.560
Ah! Grilled mandarin oranges!

00:15:20.730 --> 00:15:24.650
I'll have some! They taste even better
around this time of year, don't they?

00:15:24.650 --> 00:15:27.650
You sure like mandarin oranges,
don't you, Chika-<i>chan</i>?

00:15:27.860 --> 00:15:29.470
Yep! I love them!

00:15:29.780 --> 00:15:36.230
Every time I eat one, I think,
"Ahh... I'm so glad...

00:15:36.990 --> 00:15:38.330
...that I was born here!"

00:15:39.040 --> 00:15:42.920
At any rate, this place hasn't changed.

00:15:43.040 --> 00:15:46.090
No. Even the scent it gives off
hasn't changed a bit.

00:15:46.090 --> 00:15:47.170
Scent?

00:15:47.170 --> 00:15:52.050
Yeah. Since you go to school every day,
you may not realize it,

00:15:52.050 --> 00:15:53.180
but this place has a scent...

00:15:53.640 --> 00:15:56.310
A scent that brings back memories...

00:16:03.600 --> 00:16:06.360
Hm? What's that sound?

00:16:06.360 --> 00:16:07.690
Yeah, I can hear it, too.

00:16:07.900 --> 00:16:10.570
Hey! Chika!

00:16:10.860 --> 00:16:13.070
Can you come over here?!

00:16:13.070 --> 00:16:14.280
Well then!

00:16:16.330 --> 00:16:19.950
Yoshimi-<i>chan</i>! What is it?!

00:16:19.950 --> 00:16:21.040
You'll see.

00:16:21.120 --> 00:16:22.250
What is it?

00:16:22.250 --> 00:16:23.870
Ta-da!

00:16:26.340 --> 00:16:28.050
Wow...!

00:16:32.220 --> 00:16:33.430
Come see it!

00:16:33.430 --> 00:16:35.220
What is it?

00:16:35.640 --> 00:16:37.060
Wow...!

00:16:40.390 --> 00:16:42.520
Yay!

00:16:40.390 --> 00:16:49.860
"Thank you, Ura High"

00:16:52.860 --> 00:16:55.820
Do you like it?! You're 
surprised, aren't you?!

00:16:55.950 --> 00:16:58.160
Yep! I love it!

00:16:58.160 --> 00:17:00.810
We've got more coming!

00:17:01.870 --> 00:17:03.540
One, two...!

00:17:38.990 --> 00:17:43.330
Time flies when you're having fun...

00:17:44.120 --> 00:17:50.340
Everyone wishes that
fun times could last forever.

00:17:50.880 --> 00:17:53.590
But it always comes to an end after all.

00:17:53.590 --> 00:17:56.050
"Winner"

00:17:54.380 --> 00:17:56.050
We can't turn back time,

00:17:56.840 --> 00:17:59.800
nor can we re-live moments in time...

00:18:00.430 --> 00:18:02.590
In a way, it's really sad, but...

00:18:03.430 --> 00:18:07.310
At the same time,
we're also kind of looking forward

00:18:07.310 --> 00:18:09.480
to seeing what tomorrow will bring.

00:18:10.690 --> 00:18:17.310
That truly makes us aware
of the passage of time, <i>zura</i>.

00:18:22.700 --> 00:18:24.410
And then, we notice...

00:18:25.500 --> 00:18:28.920
...that perhaps it is precisely because
this time will never come again

00:18:29.250 --> 00:18:32.640
that we can truly enjoy
this moment for what it is.

00:18:33.880 --> 00:18:35.920
It's because we know...

00:18:36.260 --> 00:18:39.010
...that what is happening now
will never happen again,

00:18:39.930 --> 00:18:41.430
that we can do our very best.

00:18:43.760 --> 00:18:48.250
Because we all know
things will come to an end someday...

00:18:49.940 --> 00:18:55.330
Because we all know that tomorrow
will still come even after it's over...

00:19:04.540 --> 00:19:08.910
Because we have to start
walking towards the future...!

00:19:15.960 --> 00:19:19.740
That's probably why... everyone smiles.

00:19:52.790 --> 00:19:56.960
This concludes the Uranohoshi Girls'
High's School Closing Festival.

00:19:57.880 --> 00:20:02.190
Watching the people who came
to the festival today, I've re-realized...

00:20:03.220 --> 00:20:06.000
...how much this school was loved...

00:20:06.680 --> 00:20:11.730
...and how important it was
to this town... and to all of us...

00:20:13.100 --> 00:20:13.990
So...

00:20:14.690 --> 00:20:16.730
...this School Closing Festival...

00:20:16.730 --> 00:20:20.470
...made me... the happiest...

00:20:21.360 --> 00:20:25.210
I felt a warmth stronger
than I've ever felt before...

00:20:27.160 --> 00:20:28.660
Mari-<i>san</i>...

00:20:30.200 --> 00:20:31.620
I'm sorry.

00:20:33.750 --> 00:20:34.710
Mari...

00:20:36.130 --> 00:20:37.310
I'm sorry...

00:20:37.920 --> 00:20:39.120
I'm sorry...

00:20:40.340 --> 00:20:44.510
If I had tried just a bit harder...
Just a bit harder...

00:20:48.930 --> 00:20:55.100
Aqours...! Aqours...! Aqours...!

00:20:55.100 --> 00:21:01.400
--Aqours...! Aqours...! Aqours...!
--Aqours...! Aqours...! Aqours...!

00:21:01.400 --> 00:21:07.910
Aqours...! Aqours...! Aqours...!

00:21:07.910 --> 00:21:13.960
Aqours...! Aqours...! Aqours...!

00:21:13.960 --> 00:21:19.590
Aqours...! Aqours...! Aqours...!

00:21:28.800 --> 00:21:30.930
Thank you, everyone!

00:21:32.680 --> 00:21:37.190
Well then, let's finish things
by singing together!

00:21:37.190 --> 00:21:39.060
With all our cheer!

00:21:39.440 --> 00:21:41.570
With all our joy!

00:21:41.940 --> 00:21:44.800
Sing so loud it reaches the heavens!

00:21:45.570 --> 00:21:48.450
<i>Try and be brave</i>

00:21:48.450 --> 00:21:50.990
<i>I know it's actually scary</i>

00:21:50.990 --> 00:21:57.000
<i>It's not like I was able</i>
<i>to</i> <i>do it from the start, either</i>

00:21:57.000 --> 00:21:59.840
<i>I messed up a lot</i>

00:21:59.840 --> 00:22:02.500
<i>I was really frustrated</i>

00:22:02.500 --> 00:22:08.050
<i>But</i> <i>that</i> <i>gave</i> <i>me</i> <i>strength,</i>
<i>so</i> <i>just</i> <i>don't</i> <i>give</i> <i>up</i>

00:22:08.050 --> 00:22:13.770
<i>Tears</i> <i>in</i> <i>your</i> <i>eyes</i>
<i>that</i> <i>want</i> <i>to</i> <i>try</i> <i>believing</i>

00:22:13.770 --> 00:22:18.020
<i>Say "bye-bye" to hesitation and tears</i>

00:22:18.020 --> 00:22:19.690
<i>Now, let's go!</i>

00:22:19.690 --> 00:22:24.860
<i>Let's chase them as</i> <i>many</i> <i>times</i>
<i>as it takes, don't lose</i>

00:22:24.860 --> 00:22:28.110
<i>Everyone fails sometimes</i>

00:22:28.110 --> 00:22:31.160
<i>But dreams won't fade, dreams won't fade</i>

00:22:31.160 --> 00:22:36.540
<i>Let's chase them as</i> <i>many</i> <i>times</i>
<i>as it takes, don't lose</i>

00:22:36.540 --> 00:22:46.010
<i>'Cause today is today, and once</i>
<i>you</i> <i>wake up, it'll be a new morning</i>

00:22:57.310 --> 00:23:03.820
♪ "We did everything that we could do" ♪

00:23:03.820 --> 00:23:10.240
♪ It'd be nice to be able 
to say that someday ♪

00:23:10.240 --> 00:23:27.720
♪ But that day's still far away, so until then,
we'll do our best and keep trying ♪

00:23:36.140 --> 00:23:41.450
"#12 'Sea of Light'"

00:23:36.270 --> 00:23:40.620
Next Time! "Sea of Light."
